{"id":"CVE-2010-2790","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2010-08-04T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T02:46:48.224Z","description":"Multiple cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities in the formatQuery function in frontends/php/include/classes/class.curl.php in Zabbix before 1.8.3rc1 allow remote attackers to inject arbitrary web script or HTML via the (1) filter_set, (2) show_details, (3) filter_rst, or (4) txt_select parameters to the triggers page (tr_status.php).  NOTE: some of these details are obtained from third party information.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.zabbix.com/forum/showthread.php?p=68770","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/60772","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"zabbix-classcurl-xss(60772)"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2010/1908","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2010-1908"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/40679","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"40679"},{"url":"https://support.zabbix.com/browse/ZBX-2326","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/42017","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"42017"}],"vendors":["curl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2010-3842","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2010-10-27T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T03:26:12.269Z","description":"Absolute path traversal vulnerability in curl 7.20.0 through 7.21.1, when the --remote-header-name or -J option is used, allows remote servers to create or overwrite arbitrary files by using \\ (backslash) as a separator of path components within the Content-disposition HTTP header.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://curl.haxx.se/docs/adv_20101013.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2010/10/13/4","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20101013 Re: CVE Request -- cURL / mingw32-cURL -- Did not strip directory parts separated by backslashes, when downloading files"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2010/10/13/5","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20101013 Re: CVE Request -- cURL / mingw32-cURL -- Did not strip directory parts separated by backslashes, when downloading files"},{"url":"http://securitytracker.com/id?1024583","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1024583"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/39532","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"39532"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2010/10/13/1","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20101013 CVE Request -- cURL / mingw32-cURL -- Did not strip directory parts separated by backslashes, when downloading files"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=642642","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["curl"]}
